#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Introduction to cryptographic hashing {#introduction-to-cryptographic-"
"hashing}"
msgstr ""
"Pengenalan hashing kriptografi {#introduction-to-cryptographic-hashing}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Hash "
"functions](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Cryptographic_hash_function&oldid=1159000809)"
" represent a valuable construct in cryptography as they help enable "
"validation with confidentiality. As such, hash functions form an important "
"component of mechanisms for data authentication and integrity, such as "
"[hash-based message authentication "
"codes](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=HMAC&oldid=1158164088) "
"(HMAC) and [digital "
"signatures](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_signature&oldid=1161173191)."
" This article will discuss the basic ideas and security considerations "
"underpinning cryptographic hash functions and outline potential "
"vulnerabilities from the advent of quantum computing.\n"
msgstr ""
"[Fungsi "
"hash](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Cryptographic_hash_function&oldid=1159000809)"
" merupakan konstruk yang berharga dalam kriptografi karena membantu "
"memungkinkan validasi dengan kerahasiaan. Sebagai demikian, fungsi hash "
"merupakan komponen penting dari mekanisme autentikasi dan integritas data, "
"seperti [hash-based message authentication "
"codes](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=HMAC&oldid=1158164088) "
"(HMAC) dan [tanda tangan "
"digital](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_signature&oldid=1161173191)."
" Artikel ini akan membahas ide-ide dasar dan pertimbangan keamanan yang "
"mendasari fungsi hash kriptografi serta menguraikan potensi kerentanan dari "
"munculnya komputasi kuantum.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Basic rationale and design of hash functions {#basic-rationale-and-design-"
"of-hash-functions}"
msgstr ""
"Dasar pemikiran dan desain fungsi hash {#basic-rationale-and-design-of-hash-"
"functions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are many situations where authentication and integrity verification "
"need to be performed cheaply and without revealing private information to "
"the party performing the validation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ada banyak situasi di mana autentikasi dan verifikasi integritas perlu "
"dilakukan secara murah dan tanpa mengungkapkan informasi privat kepada pihak"
" yang melakukan validasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, when downloading software from a remote server, an efficient "
"mechanism is needed to verify that the software actually downloaded has not "
"been modified since being created by the original author of the software. "
"Similarly, when authenticating users of web applications, it would be "
"desirable to use a mechanism that does not involve physically storing or "
"transmitting the actual passwords, which can potentially compromise their "
"confidentiality.\n"
msgstr ""
"Misalnya, saat mengunduh perangkat lunak dari server jarak jauh, diperlukan "
"mekanisme yang efisien untuk memverifikasi bahwa perangkat lunak yang "
"diunduh belum dimodifikasi sejak dibuat oleh penulis asli perangkat lunak "
"tersebut. Demikian pula, saat mengautentikasi pengguna aplikasi web, akan "
"lebih baik menggunakan mekanisme yang tidak melibatkan penyimpanan fisik "
"atau transmisi kata sandi yang sebenarnya, yang berpotensi membahayakan "
"kerahasiaannya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Cryptographic hash functions* (CHFs) address such needs efficiently and "
"securely.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Fungsi hash kriptografi* (CHF) memenuhi kebutuhan tersebut secara efisien "
"dan aman.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Fundamentally, a cryptographic hash function takes an input (or *message*) of arbitrary length and returns a fixed-size string of n-bits as output. The output of a <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Cryptographic hash functions take an input (or message) and produce a fixed-size output, which is typically a string of characters of a fixed length.\">CHF</DefinitionTooltip> is also referred to as a *digest*.\n"
"A useful CHF should satisfy several key properties:\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada dasarnya, fungsi hash kriptografi mengambil input (atau *pesan*) dengan panjang sembarang dan mengembalikan string n-bit berukuran tetap sebagai output. Output dari sebuah <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Fungsi hash kriptografi mengambil input (atau pesan) dan menghasilkan output berukuran tetap, yang biasanya berupa string karakter dengan panjang tetap.\">CHF</DefinitionTooltip> juga disebut sebagai *digest*.\n"
"CHF yang berguna harus memenuhi beberapa properti kunci:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Uniformity:** The digests produced by a CHF should be distributed "
"uniformly and should look random. The aim is to ensure the output leaks no "
"information about the input.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Keseragaman:** Digest yang dihasilkan oleh CHF harus terdistribusi secara "
"seragam dan terlihat acak. Tujuannya adalah memastikan output tidak "
"membocorkan informasi apa pun tentang input.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Determinism:** For a given input, a CHF must always produce the same "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Refers to a fixed-length string or hash "
"value generated from input data of arbitrary "
"size.\">digest</DefinitionTooltip>, that is, it must be deterministic.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Determinisme:** Untuk input yang diberikan, CHF harus selalu menghasilkan "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Mengacu pada string atau nilai hash panjang-"
"tetap yang dihasilkan dari data input berukuran "
"sembarang.\">digest</DefinitionTooltip> yang sama, yaitu, harus "
"deterministik.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Irreversibility:** A CHF is a <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A "
"mathematical function that is relatively easy to compute in one direction "
"but extremely difficult to reverse.\">*one-way function*</DefinitionTooltip>"
" in that, given a digest, it should be infeasible to invert the hashing and "
"obtain the input.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Tidak dapat dibalik:** CHF adalah <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Fungsi "
"matematika yang relatif mudah dihitung dalam satu arah tetapi sangat sulit "
"dibalik.\">*fungsi satu arah*</DefinitionTooltip> dalam artian bahwa, "
"diberikan sebuah digest, seharusnya tidak mungkin (secara komputasional) "
"untuk membalik proses hashing dan mendapatkan inputnya.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Approximate injectivity:** While CHFs are many-to-one functions, they "
"should appear to look like one-to one functions. This is achieved by "
"combining an enormous output space size with the avalanche effect whereby "
"tiny changes in the input lead to wildly divergent digests.  This "
"characteristic is known as approximate injectivity.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Injektivitas perkiraan:** Meskipun CHF adalah fungsi banyak-ke-satu, "
"mereka harus terlihat seperti fungsi satu-ke-satu. Ini dicapai dengan "
"menggabungkan ukuran ruang output yang sangat besar dengan efek avalanche di"
" mana perubahan kecil pada input menyebabkan digest yang sangat berbeda. "
"Karakteristik ini dikenal sebagai injektivitas perkiraan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given this, it's possible to validate a piece of data against the original instance by comparing a digest of the data to a digest of the original.\n"
" - If the two digests match, we can be confident with high probability that the data is identical to the original.\n"
" - If the digests differ, we can be sure that the data was tampered with or is otherwise inauthentic.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berdasarkan ini, memungkinkan untuk memvalidasi sepotong data terhadap instansi asli dengan membandingkan digest dari data dengan digest dari aslinya.\n"
" - Jika dua digest cocok, kita bisa yakin dengan probabilitas tinggi bahwa data identik dengan aslinya.\n"
" - Jika digest berbeda, kita bisa yakin bahwa data telah dirusak atau tidak otentik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since the CHF digests themselves do not reveal the actual contents of the "
"data or the original, they enable validation while preserving privacy.\n"
msgstr ""
"Karena digest CHF itu sendiri tidak mengungkapkan konten sebenarnya dari "
"data atau aslinya, mereka memungkinkan validasi sambil menjaga privasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<Accordion>\n"
msgstr "<Accordion>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<AccordionItem title=\"<en>Mathematical description</en>\">\n"
msgstr "<AccordionItem title=\"<en>Mathematical description</en>\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "A hash function $H$ can be defined as:\n"
msgstr "A hash function $H$ can be defined as:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$H : Σ^* \\rightarrow \\{0,1\\}^n$\n"
msgstr "$H : Σ^* \\rightarrow \\{0,1\\}^n$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $Σ^*$ is the set of all possible strings which we may consider to be "
"binary strings of any length.\n"
msgstr ""
"where $Σ^*$ is the set of all possible strings which we may consider to be "
"binary strings of any length.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The fact that the size of the input domain $Σ^*$ of $H$ is unbounded while "
"that of the co-domain $\\{0,1\\}^n$ is bounded means that $H$ is necessarily"
" many-to-one mapping infinitely many inputs to any given n-bit string.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fakta bahwa ukuran domain input $Σ^*$ dari $H$ tidak terbatas sementara ko-"
"domain $\\{0,1\\}^n$ terbatas berarti bahwa $H$ secara inheren merupakan "
"pemetaan banyak-ke-satu yang memetakan tak hingga banyak input ke string "
"n-bit mana pun.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The properties of uniformity and determinism are nicely encapsulated within "
"the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"An idealized cryptographic model often "
"used in theoretical discussions and analyses of cryptographic protocols and "
"schemes, it allows for clear and rigorous analysis of security "
"properties.\">*random oracle model*</DefinitionTooltip> of cryptographic "
"hashing.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sifat uniformitas dan determinisme terangkum dengan baik dalam "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Model kriptografi yang diidealisasikan yang "
"sering digunakan dalam diskusi teoritis dan analisis protokol serta skema "
"kriptografi; memungkinkan analisis sifat keamanan yang jelas dan "
"ketat.\">*model oracle acak*</DefinitionTooltip> dari hashing kriptografi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Example of cryptographic hashing in Python with SHA-256 {#example-of-"
"cryptographic-hashing-in-python-with-sha-256}"
msgstr ""
"Contoh hashing kriptografi di Python dengan SHA-256 {#example-of-"
"cryptographic-hashing-in-python-with-sha-256}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This simple example demonstrates cryptographic hashing using the popular [SHA-256](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=SHA-2&oldid=1155462953) algorithm as provided by the `cryptography` Python library.\n"
"First we show how a minor difference in plain texts leads to a very large difference in the hash digests.\n"
msgstr ""
"Contoh sederhana ini mendemonstrasikan hashing kriptografi menggunakan algoritma [SHA-256](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=SHA-2&oldid=1155462953) yang populer seperti yang disediakan oleh library Python `cryptography`.\n"
"Pertama kita tunjukkan bagaimana perbedaan kecil dalam plain text menghasilkan perbedaan yang sangat besar dalam digest hash.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The two messages differ in exactly one character.\n"
msgstr "Dua pesan berbeda persis satu karakter.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we instantiate `hash` objects to enable the hashing process, which "
"involves calls to two methods: `update` and `finalize`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya, kita instansiasi objek `hash` untuk mengaktifkan proses "
"hashing, yang melibatkan panggilan ke dua metode: `update` dan `finalize`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We see that due to the avalanche effect in the SHA-256 CHF, a one-character "
"difference in input messages yields two very different digests.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita melihat bahwa karena efek avalanche dalam SHA-256 CHF, perbedaan satu "
"karakter dalam pesan input menghasilkan dua digest yang sangat berbeda.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applications of cryptographic hashing {#applications-of-cryptographic-"
"hashing}"
msgstr "Aplikasi hashing kriptografi {#applications-of-cryptographic-hashing}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The unique properties of CHFs make them suitable for a wide array of "
"applications:\n"
msgstr "Properti unik dari CHF membuatnya cocok untuk berbagai aplikasi:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Data integrity checks:** Hash functions can be used to create a "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Commonly used technique in cryptography to "
"detect errors during data transmission involving adding a value(which is "
"often derived from the data itself) to the data to create a checksum value. "
"The recipient can then perform the same calculation to compare checksums to "
"verify authenticity.\">checksum</DefinitionTooltip> for a set of data. Any "
"modifications to the data, intentional or not, will result in a different "
"checksum, alerting systems or users to the change. The checksum is also "
"typically much more compact than the original data, which makes checksum "
"comparisons very fast.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pemeriksaan integritas data:** Fungsi hash bisa digunakan untuk membuat "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Teknik yang umum digunakan dalam kriptografi"
" untuk mendeteksi error selama transmisi data yang melibatkan penambahan "
"nilai (yang sering berasal dari data itu sendiri) ke data untuk membuat "
"nilai checksum. Penerima kemudian bisa melakukan perhitungan yang sama untuk"
" membandingkan checksum guna memverifikasi "
"keaslian.\">checksum</DefinitionTooltip> untuk sekumpulan data. Setiap "
"modifikasi pada data, baik disengaja maupun tidak, akan menghasilkan "
"checksum yang berbeda, memperingatkan sistem atau pengguna tentang perubahan"
" tersebut. Checksum juga biasanya jauh lebih ringkas dari data asli, yang "
"membuat perbandingan checksum menjadi sangat cepat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Fig 1: Secure hashing for data integrity "
"checks](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/cryptographic-"
"hash-functions/data-integrity.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Gambar 1: Hashing aman untuk pemeriksaan integritas "
"data](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/cryptographic-hash-"
"functions/data-integrity.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Figure 1. Secure hashing for data integrity*\n"
msgstr "*Gambar 1. Hashing aman untuk integritas data*\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Digital signatures:** Cryptographic hashes are essential to the "
"functioning of digital signatures as they involve comparing "
"cryptographically hashed messages to establish authenticity and integrity "
"while preserving privacy.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Tanda tangan digital:** Hash kriptografi sangat penting untuk berfungsinya"
" tanda tangan digital karena melibatkan perbandingan pesan yang di-hash "
"secara kriptografi untuk menetapkan keaslian dan integritas sambil menjaga "
"privasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Fig 2: Digital signatures](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/cryptographic-hash-functions/digital-signature.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Gambar 2: Tanda tangan digital](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/cryptographic-hash-functions/digital-signature.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Figure 2. Digital signatures*\n"
msgstr "*Gambar 2. Tanda tangan digital*\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Blockchain and cryptocurrencies:** Cryptocurrencies like Bitcoin rely "
"heavily on CHFs, particularly in creating transaction integrity and enabling"
" consensus mechanisms like *proof of work*.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Blockchain dan mata uang kripto:** Mata uang kripto seperti Bitcoin sangat"
" mengandalkan CHF, khususnya dalam menciptakan integritas transaksi dan "
"memungkinkan mekanisme konsensus seperti *proof of work*.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Security of cryptographic hashing {#security-of-cryptographic-hashing}"
msgstr "Keamanan hashing kriptografi {#security-of-cryptographic-hashing}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The security of a CHF is typically assessed based on resistance to two types"
" of attacks: [pre-"
"image](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Preimage_attack&oldid=1145879411)"
" and "
"[collision](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Collision_attack&oldid=1138239916).\n"
msgstr ""
"Keamanan CHF biasanya dinilai berdasarkan ketahanan terhadap dua jenis "
"serangan: [pre-"
"image](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Preimage_attack&oldid=1145879411)"
" dan "
"[collision](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Collision_attack&oldid=1138239916).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Pre-image resistance {#pre-image-resistance}"
msgstr "Ketahanan pre-image {#pre-image-resistance}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Pre-image resistance* means that given a digest, it should be infeasible to"
" find the input.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Ketahanan pre-image* berarti bahwa diberikan sebuah digest, harus tidak "
"mungkin menemukan inputnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This is related to the one-way property of CHFs.\n"
msgstr "Ini terkait dengan properti satu arah dari CHF.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A good CHF is designed in such a way that a party wishing to conduct a pre-"
"image attack has no better option than a brute force approach, which has "
"time complexity $2^n$.\n"
msgstr ""
"CHF yang baik dirancang sedemikian rupa sehingga pihak yang ingin melakukan "
"serangan pre-image tidak memiliki pilihan yang lebih baik selain pendekatan "
"brute force, yang memiliki kompleksitas waktu $2^n$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<AccordionItem title=\"<em>Mathematical details</em>\">\n"
msgstr "<AccordionItem title=\"<em>Detail matematis</em>\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given a CHF $H$ and digest $g$, it should be computationally infeasible to "
"find any input $m$ from the pre-image of $g$ whereby $H(m) = g$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Diberikan CHF $H$ dan digest $g$, seharusnya tidak mungkin secara komputasi "
"untuk menemukan input $m$ mana pun dari pre-image $g$ sedemikian sehingga "
"$H(m) = g$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Collision resistance {#collision-resistance}"
msgstr "Ketahanan collision {#collision-resistance}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Collision resistance* means that it is difficult to find two different "
"inputs that hash to the same digest.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Ketahanan collision* berarti bahwa sulit menemukan dua input berbeda yang "
"di-hash ke digest yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A *cryptographic hash collision* occurs when two inputs hash to the same "
"digest. While collisions inevitably exist given the many-to-one nature of "
"CHFs, a good CHF nevertheless makes it infeasible to locate one at will.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebuah *collision hash kriptografi* terjadi ketika dua input di-hash ke "
"digest yang sama. Meskipun collision pasti ada mengingat sifat banyak-ke-"
"satu dari CHF, namun CHF yang baik tetap membuatnya tidak mungkin untuk "
"menemukan satu sesuai keinginan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Collision resistance is crucial for applications like digital signatures and"
" certificates, where it could be disastrous if a malicious party were able "
"to create a forgery that hashes to the same value.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ketahanan collision sangat penting untuk aplikasi seperti tanda tangan "
"digital dan sertifikat, di mana akan sangat berbahaya jika pihak yang tidak "
"bertanggung jawab bisa membuat pemalsuan yang di-hash ke nilai yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<AccordionItem title=\"<em>Mathematical details of hash collisions</em>\">\n"
msgstr "<AccordionItem title=\"<em>Detail matematis collision hash</em>\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid " $m_1, m_2$ can be found such that $H(m_1) = H(m_2)$.\n"
msgstr " $m_1, m_2$ can be found such that $H(m_1) = H(m_2)$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hash length {#hash-length}"
msgstr "Panjang hash {#hash-length}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Collision resistance is a harder requirement than pre-image resistance and "
"necessitates output lengths twice as long as that needed for pre-image "
"resistance. This is because a brute force attack known as the [birthday "
"attack](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Birthday_attack&oldid=1161075943),"
" which can be used to identify hash collisions, has time complexity "
"$2^{n/2}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ketahanan collision adalah persyaratan yang lebih sulit daripada ketahanan "
"pre-image dan memerlukan panjang output dua kali lebih panjang dari yang "
"dibutuhkan untuk ketahanan pre-image. Ini karena serangan brute force yang "
"dikenal sebagai [birthday "
"attack](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Birthday_attack&oldid=1161075943),"
" yang bisa digunakan untuk mengidentifikasi hash collision, memiliki "
"kompleksitas waktu $2^{n/2}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the absence of cryptanalytic weaknesses, the security of a hash function "
"is therefore primarily influenced by its hash length. The longer the hash, "
"the more secure it is, as it becomes harder to mount brute force attacks.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tanpa adanya kelemahan kriptanalisis, keamanan fungsi hash oleh karena itu "
"terutama dipengaruhi oleh panjang hash-nya. Semakin panjang hash, semakin "
"aman, karena semakin sulit untuk melancarkan serangan brute force.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Commonly used cryptographic hash functions {#commonly-used-cryptographic-"
"hash-functions}"
msgstr ""
"Fungsi hash kriptografi yang umum digunakan {#commonly-used-cryptographic-"
"hash-functions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following table lists some commonly used cryptographic hash functions, "
"along with their hash lengths and primary application domains:\n"
msgstr ""
"Tabel berikut mencantumkan beberapa fungsi hash kriptografi yang umum "
"digunakan, beserta panjang hash dan domain aplikasi utamanya:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Hash Function | Output Length (bits) | Common Applications                                        |\n"
"|---------------|----------------------|------------------------------------------------------------|\n"
"| MD5           | 128                  | File integrity checking, older systems, non-crypto uses    |\n"
"| SHA-1         | 160                  | Legacy systems, Git for version control                    |\n"
"| SHA-256       | 256                  | Cryptocurrency (Bitcoin), digital signatures, certificates |\n"
"| SHA-3         | Variable (up to 512) | Various cryptographic applications, successor to SHA-2     |\n"
"| Blake2        | Variable (up to 512) | Cryptography, replacing MD5/SHA-1 in some systems          |\n"
"| Blake3        | Variable (up to 256) | Cryptography, file hashing, data integrity                 |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Fungsi Hash | Panjang Output (bit) | Aplikasi Umum                                              |\n"
"|-------------|----------------------|------------------------------------------------------------|\n"
"| MD5         | 128                  | Pemeriksaan integritas file, sistem lama, penggunaan non-kriptografi |\n"
"| SHA-1       | 160                  | Sistem lama, Git untuk version control                     |\n"
"| SHA-256     | 256                  | Mata uang kripto (Bitcoin), tanda tangan digital, sertifikat |\n"
"| SHA-3       | Variabel (hingga 512) | Berbagai aplikasi kriptografi, penerus SHA-2              |\n"
"| Blake2      | Variabel (hingga 512) | Kriptografi, menggantikan MD5/SHA-1 di beberapa sistem    |\n"
"| Blake3      | Variabel (hingga 256) | Kriptografi, hashing file, integritas data                |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- [MD5](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=MD5&oldid=1161719955) and [SHA-1](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=SHA-1&oldid=1161401043), while still seen in less sensitive applications places, are considered deprecated in terms of collision resistance and are not recommended for new systems.\n"
"SHA-256, part of the [SHA-2](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=SHA-2&oldid=1155462953) family, is widely used and currently secure for most applications.\n"
"- [SHA-3](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=SHA-3&oldid=1161463128) is a newer standard that was selected by NIST in 2015 as the winner of the NIST hash function competition. It's designed to be a drop-in replacement for SHA-2, but it also has some different internal characteristics and is resistant to certain types of attacks that might be effective against SHA-2.\n"
"- [Blake2 and Blake3](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=BLAKE_(hash_function)&oldid=1161463384) are cryptographic hash functions that are faster than MD5, SHA-1, SHA-2, and SHA-3, but at least as secure as the latest standard, SHA-3. They are increasingly being used in new systems, particularly where speed is important.\n"
msgstr ""
"- [MD5](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=MD5&oldid=1161719955) dan [SHA-1](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=SHA-1&oldid=1161401043), meskipun masih terlihat di aplikasi yang kurang sensitif, dianggap sudah usang dalam hal ketahanan collision dan tidak direkomendasikan untuk sistem baru.\n"
"SHA-256, bagian dari keluarga [SHA-2](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=SHA-2&oldid=1155462953), banyak digunakan dan saat ini aman untuk sebagian besar aplikasi.\n"
"- [SHA-3](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=SHA-3&oldid=1161463128) adalah standar yang lebih baru yang dipilih oleh NIST pada tahun 2015 sebagai pemenang kompetisi fungsi hash NIST. Dirancang sebagai pengganti drop-in untuk SHA-2, tetapi juga memiliki beberapa karakteristik internal yang berbeda dan tahan terhadap jenis serangan tertentu yang mungkin efektif terhadap SHA-2.\n"
"- [Blake2 dan Blake3](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=BLAKE_(hash_function)&oldid=1161463384) adalah fungsi hash kriptografi yang lebih cepat dari MD5, SHA-1, SHA-2, dan SHA-3, tetapi setidaknya seaman standar terbaru, SHA-3. Mereka semakin banyak digunakan dalam sistem baru, terutama di mana kecepatan penting.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum risks to traditional cryptographic hashing {#quantum-risks-to-"
"traditional-cryptographic-hashing}"
msgstr ""
"Risiko kuantum terhadap hashing kriptografi tradisional {#quantum-risks-to-"
"traditional-cryptographic-hashing}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The primary quantum threat to cryptographic hashing is posed by brute force "
"attacks.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ancaman kuantum utama terhadap hashing kriptografi ditimbulkan oleh serangan"
" brute force.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given a particular digest, an attacker will try out random inputs until they"
" locate one which produces the same digest.\n"
msgstr ""
"Diberikan digest tertentu, penyerang akan mencoba input acak sampai "
"menemukan satu yang menghasilkan digest yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With $n$ bits in the input, there are $2^n$ possible values. Therefore, the "
"attacker needs to try out around $2^{n-1}$ inputs to have a better than 50% "
"chance of success.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan $n$ bit dalam input, ada $2^n$ kemungkinan nilai. Oleh karena itu, "
"penyerang perlu mencoba sekitar $2^{n-1}$ input untuk memiliki kemungkinan "
"sukses lebih dari 50%.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Grover's algorithm {#grovers-algorithm}"
msgstr "Algoritma Grover {#grovers-algorithm}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For such an unstructured search context, Grover's algorithm can provide a "
"quadratic speedup using a technique known as <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Technique used in algorithms to leverage certain phenomenons in"
" the quantum interface which increase the probability (amplitude) of the "
"correct answer when searching through a large set of "
"possibilities/definitions.\">quantum amplitude "
"amplification</DefinitionTooltip>, reducing the time complexity of a pre-"
"image attack to $2^{n/2}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk konteks pencarian tidak terstruktur seperti ini, algoritma Grover bisa"
" memberikan percepatan kuadratik menggunakan teknik yang dikenal sebagai "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Teknik yang digunakan dalam algoritma untuk "
"memanfaatkan fenomena tertentu dalam antarmuka kuantum yang meningkatkan "
"probabilitas (amplitudo) dari jawaban yang benar saat mencari melalui "
"sekumpulan besar kemungkinan/definisi.\">amplifikasi amplitudo "
"kuantum</DefinitionTooltip>, mengurangi kompleksitas waktu serangan pre-"
"image menjadi $2^{n/2}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In practical terms, this means that a 256-bit CHF, which is currently "
"considered secure against pre-image attacks by classical computers, would "
"provide the same level of security as a 128-bit CHF when faced with a "
"quantum attacker utilizing Grover's algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara praktis, ini berarti bahwa CHF 256-bit, yang saat ini dianggap aman "
"terhadap serangan pre-image oleh komputer klasik, akan memberikan tingkat "
"keamanan yang sama dengan CHF 128-bit ketika dihadapi dengan penyerang "
"kuantum yang menggunakan algoritma Grover.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Grover's algorithm by itself is not known to provide additional quantum "
"speedups with respect to collision attacks beyond the limit set by the "
"[birthday "
"attack](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Birthday_attack&oldid=1161075943),"
" which can be carried out on classical computers. Since the classical "
"birthday attack already requires CHFs to employ hash lengths that are twice "
"as long as needed for pre-image resistance, the fact that Grover search "
"effectively halves the hash length with respect to pre-image attacks does "
"not pose a practical threat.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Grover sendiri tidak diketahui memberikan percepatan kuantum "
"tambahan sehubungan dengan serangan collision di luar batas yang ditetapkan "
"oleh [birthday "
"attack](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Birthday_attack&oldid=1161075943),"
" yang bisa dilakukan pada komputer klasik. Karena birthday attack klasik "
"sudah mengharuskan CHF menggunakan panjang hash dua kali lebih panjang dari "
"yang diperlukan untuk ketahanan pre-image, fakta bahwa pencarian Grover "
"secara efektif mengurangi setengah panjang hash sehubungan dengan serangan "
"pre-image tidak menimbulkan ancaman praktis.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, in the case of SHA-256, performing on the order of $2^{128}$ "
"operations to execute a Grover-assisted pre-image attack would still be "
"infeasible in the foreseeable future.\n"
msgstr ""
"Misalnya, dalam kasus SHA-256, melakukan sekitar $2^{128}$ operasi untuk "
"menjalankan serangan pre-image yang dibantu Grover tetap tidak dapat "
"dilakukan dalam waktu mendatang.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "BHT algorithm {#bht-algorithm}"
msgstr "Algoritma BHT {#bht-algorithm}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A quantum algorithm that combines aspects of the birthday attack with Grover"
" search was proposed in 1997 by [Brassard, Høyer, and "
"Tapp](http://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/9705002) (BHT) and affords a theoretical"
" scaling of $O(2^{n/3})$ for finding hash collisions. However, this improved"
" scaling is predicated on the existence of quantum random access memory "
"[QRAM](http://arxiv.org/abs/2205.14023) technology, which currently does not"
" exist.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma kuantum yang menggabungkan aspek birthday attack dengan pencarian "
"Grover diusulkan pada tahun 1997 oleh [Brassard, Høyer, dan "
"Tapp](http://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/9705002) (BHT) dan memberikan skala "
"teoretis $O(2^{n/3})$ untuk menemukan hash collision. Namun, peningkatan "
"skala ini bergantung pada keberadaan teknologi "
"[QRAM](http://arxiv.org/abs/2205.14023) memori akses acak kuantum, yang saat"
" ini belum ada.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Without QRAM, the realizable scaling is $\\tilde{O}(2^{2n/5})$ and for hash "
"lengths currently in use, this marginal improvement in collision-finding "
"capability relative to the birthday attack does not represent a critical "
"threat.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tanpa QRAM, skala yang bisa diwujudkan adalah $\\tilde{O}(2^{2n/5})$ dan "
"untuk panjang hash yang saat ini digunakan, peningkatan marginal dalam "
"kemampuan menemukan collision relatif terhadap birthday attack ini tidak "
"mewakili ancaman kritis.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Summary {#summary}"
msgstr "Ringkasan {#summary}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Cryptographic hash functions are an essential component for ensuring data "
"integrity and privacy in digital information systems and find widespread "
"application in many contexts.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fungsi hash kriptografi adalah komponen penting untuk memastikan integritas "
"data dan privasi dalam sistem informasi digital dan banyak digunakan dalam "
"berbagai konteks.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The security requirements of CHFs are mainly understood in terms of their "
"resistance to pre-image and collision attacks. For well-designed CHFs, the "
"hash length is a good proxy for the security level.\n"
msgstr ""
"Persyaratan keamanan CHF terutama dipahami dalam hal ketahanan terhadap "
"serangan pre-image dan collision. Untuk CHF yang dirancang dengan baik, "
"panjang hash adalah proksi yang baik untuk tingkat keamanan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While the advent of quantum computers executing the Grover and BHT "
"algorithms in theory affects the pre-image and collision resistance of "
"traditional CHFs, the long hash lengths already in use today means that "
"modern cryptographic hashing algorithms, such as SHA-3, are likely to remain"
" secure barring the discovery of as-yet-unknown cryptanalytic attacks.\n"
msgstr ""
"Meskipun munculnya komputer kuantum yang mengeksekusi algoritma Grover dan "
"BHT secara teori mempengaruhi ketahanan pre-image dan collision dari CHF "
"tradisional, panjang hash yang sudah digunakan saat ini berarti bahwa "
"algoritma hashing kriptografi modern, seperti SHA-3, kemungkinan akan tetap "
"aman kecuali ditemukan serangan kriptanalitik yang belum diketahui "
"sebelumnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The relevance of CHFs lies in their role as a fundamental building block for"
" quantum-resistant cryptographic schemes, ensuring that digital information "
"remains secure even in the face of potential future advancements in quantum "
"computing algorithms and technologies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Relevansi CHF terletak pada perannya sebagai blok bangunan fundamental untuk"
" skema kriptografi yang tahan kuantum, memastikan informasi digital tetap "
"aman bahkan menghadapi potensi kemajuan masa depan dalam algoritma dan "
"teknologi komputasi kuantum.\n"
